          %p
            Assuming all requisite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+coequalizer"} (reflective) coequalizers
            exist, universal property arguments guarantee associativity isomorphisms of type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \otimes_N B) \otimes_P C \to A \otimes_N (B \otimes_P C).
          %p
            In fact, this tensor product defines composition in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            where objects or 0-cells are monoids in a monoidal category, where 1-cells
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            bimodules, and where 2-cells from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are morphisms of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            bimodules.
          %p
            This in turn can be seen as a special case of a bicategory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with suitably nice cocompleteness properties – see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidally+cocomplete+category"} monoidally cocomplete category
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benabou+cosmos"} Benabou cosmos
          %h3#twosided_ideals_of_a_ring Two-sided ideals of a ring
          %p
            Every ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-bimodule," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biaction"} biaction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo ×
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)(-)(-):R \times R \times R \to R
            defined by the ternary product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %mi c
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi a
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi b
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a b c \coloneqq a \cdot b \cdot c
            for elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
