          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              As this notation suggests,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi BMod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} BMod
              is naturally the vertical category of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo+double+category"} pseudo double category
              whose horizontal composition is given by tensor product of bimodules.
          %h3#AsMorphismsInA2Category The 2-category of rings, bimodules, and intertwiners
          %p
            Consider bimodules over
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
          #AlgebrasAndBimodules.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                  are bimodules;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                  are
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiners"} intertwiners
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
              of 1-morphisms is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
              over the middle algebra.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
              from the above 2-category of rings and bimodules to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              which
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  sends an ring
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  to its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              %li
                %p
                  sends a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  = succeed "-bimodule" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi R
                        %mi B
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Mod
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (-)\otimes_{R} B
                        \\;\colon\;
                        Mod_{R} \to Mod_{S}
              %li
                %p
                  sends an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiner"} intertwiner
                  to the evident
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  of the above functors.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              This construction has as its image precisely the
              = succeed "-preserving" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              between
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts+theorem"} Eilenberg-Watts theorem
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              In the context of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
              one may interpret this as says that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-modules"} 2-modules
              over the given ring which are equivalent to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              is that of rings, bimodules and intertwiners. See also at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-ring"} 2-ring
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The 2-category of rings and bimodules is an archtypical example for a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+with+proarrow+equipment"} 2-category with proarrow equipment
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo+double+category"} pseudo double category
              with niche-fillers. Or in the language of
              = succeed "-theory:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} internal (infinity,1)-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mover
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo →
                        %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %munder
